<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Asser</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 909</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Asser was a Welsh monk from St <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">Davids</a> who became an adviser to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfred-the-great">Alfred the Great</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wessex">Wessex</a> and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sherborne">Sherborne</a>. In 893 he wrote a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> Life of King Alfred, the main source for Alfred's reign, which also records the submission of several south Welsh kings to Alfred in the 880s. He died around 909.</p></div>
